        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "71ccdca6-2278-5352-9b76-9cc577398d60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franklin Pierce, Lewis Cass, James Buchanan, Stephen A. Douglas, Andrew Jackson, Duncan McArthur\n- Events: 1852 Democratic National Convention, Treaty of Fort Meigs\n- Places: Michigan, Pennsylvania, Illinois\n- Organizations: United States Senate, United States of America\n- Concepts: Native American tribes, presidential nomination\n\nFacts:\n- The Treaty of Fort Meigs, also called the Treaty of the Foot of the Rapids, was signed on September 29, 1817.\n- The Treaty of Fort Meigs was signed between the United States of America, represented by Lewis Cass and Duncan McArthur, and chiefs and warriors of the Wyandot, Seneca, Delaware, Shawnee, Potawatomi, Ottawa, and Chippewa tribes.\n- Lewis Cass was an American military officer, politician, and statesman who lived from October 9, 1782 to June 17, 1866.\n- Lewis Cass represented Michigan in the United States Senate.\n- Lewis Cass served in the cabinets of Andrew Jackson and James Buchanan.\n- At the 1852 Democratic National Convention, Franklin Pierce was nominated for President as a dark horse candidate on the 49th ballot.\n- At the 1852 Democratic National Convention, Franklin Pierce was chosen over Lewis Cass of Michigan, the Democratic nominee in 1848, James Buchanan of Pennsylvania, and Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4ffc0f80-4765-5b36-bde8-a7ca423b4ba8",
        "text": "Page: 1852 Democratic National Convention. Sentence: The 1852 Democratic National Convention nominated the dark horse candidate Franklin Pierce for President on the 49th ballot, passing over better known candidates Lewis Cass of Michigan (the previous nominee in 1848), James Buchanan of Pennsylvania, and Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois.\nPage: Lewis Cass. Sentence: Lewis Cass (October 9, 1782June 17, 1866) was an American military officer, politician, and statesman.\nPage: Lewis Cass. Sentence: He represented Michigan in the United States Senate and served in the Cabinet of Andrew Jackson and James Buchanan.\nPage: Treaty of Fort Meigs. Sentence: The Treaty of Fort Meigs, also called the Treaty of the Foot of the Rapids, was signed September 29, 1817 between the chiefs and warriors of the Wyandot, Seneca, Delaware, Shawnee, Potawatomi, Ottawa and Chippewa, tribes of Native Americans and the United States of America, represented by Lewis Cass and Duncan McArthur.",
